{"claim_id": "clm_kda_mechanism", "paper_id": "pap_kimi_k3_primary", "statement": "Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) is a delta-rule linear-attention recurrence with a channel-wise forget gate (lower-bounded log-decay via scaled sigmoid, gmin=-5, vs. the unbounded negative-softplus of prior work), enabling dense Tensor-Core matmuls for both diagonal and off-diagonal chunk tiles; three KDA layers are interleaved with one full (Gated MLA) attention layer per block to preserve global interaction, since linear attention alone loses long-range fidelity.", "claim_type": "mechanistic", "scope": {"applies_to": "long_context_linear_attention", "domain": "transformer_lm_pretraining"}, "limitations": ["motivated by 1M-token context and KV-cache memory pressure at 2.8T scale; the benefit is specifically long-context throughput/memory, not short-context quality per se"], "locator": "Section 2.1.1", "extracted_at": "2026-07-28", "tags": ["attention", "linear_attention", "kernel"], "fingerprint": "2f25dfa8b0731113"}
{"claim_id": "clm_attnres_mechanism", "paper_id": "pap_kimi_k3_primary", "statement": "Attention Residuals (AttnRes) replaces uniform residual accumulation with depth-wise attention: each layer l has a learned per-layer pseudo-query vector w_l in R^d that attends (softmax, RMSNorm'd keys to prevent large-magnitude layers from dominating) over the token embedding and all preceding layers' outputs at each sequence position, retrieving a data-dependent weighted combination rather than a fixed sum; a block-partitioned approximation (N~=8 blocks) recovers most of the benefit while bounding memory/communication from O(Ld) to O(Nd).", "claim_type": "mechanistic", "scope": {"applies_to": "residual_stream_depth_mixing", "domain": "transformer_lm_pretraining"}, "limitations": ["reported at 2.8T/many-layer scale; our stack's existing resid_lambdas/x0_lambdas is a much cruder 2-scalar (fixed, not softmax-retrieved) analogue, so this is a genuinely untested richer mechanism at our scale, not a re-run of an existing lever"], "locator": "Section 2.2, Eq. 8-10", "extracted_at": "2026-07-28", "tags": ["residual_stream", "depth", "architecture"], "fingerprint": "bda0274d2c167fba"}
